The simplest use offetch()is to download atext file.

fetch()retuns aPromisethat resolves to aResponseobject.

The Response object contains information about the server response.

Thejson() methodconverts a JSON response into a JavaScript object.

Independent downloads can run in parallel.

fetch()resolveswhen the server responds.

An HTTP error such as404 (Not Found)doesnotreject the Promise.

Instead, check theokproperty.

Usetry ... catchto handle errors.

This logs a promise.

You must useawaitto get the JSON.

If fetch is not working, check the console.

Then check the Network tab.

### Code Snippets

```
// Async function to download a file
async function loadText(file) {
const response = await fetch(file);
myDisplayer(await response.text());
}
// Call the async function
loadText("demo.txt");

---

